    "alert_id": "P006_VL_TIMING_PREGNANCY",
    "title": "Viral load timing in pregnant woman on ART",
    "message": "Guidelines state that HIV-positive pregnant women newly initiated on ART at ANC should have a VL test at 3 months on ART. This patient initiated ART 10 weeks ago (approximately 2.5 months) and already has a VL of 89 copies/mL, which is suppressed. While the result is reassuring, the timing appears slightly earlier than the 3-month guideline target. The next VL should follow the pregnant/breastfeeding algorithm: repeat at 3 months for pregnant and breastfeeding women if non-suppressed, or continue routine monitoring if suppressed.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "low",
    "recommended_action": "Confirm VL was done per guideline schedule. Continue routine VL monitoring per pregnancy algorithm; next VL at 6 months on ART if suppressed.",
